      "value": "@{5b81aa8964ecac2f8b14382e|full_name}: I mean... If we are going purely after performance it'd be the most senseble to just toggle gameobjects via code through one update loop. But that'd steal away some versatility, that the animators provide. Its always a trade off. I would personally much prefer the code based variant, especially because about 75% of my menu are just gameobject toggles, some swap materials aswell though, and some do blendshapes or trigger constraints.",
